## 18. EFFECTIVE LICENSING AND ACCEPTANCE

This Agreement does not, by itself, grant an Institution permission to use the Software.

A valid licence shall arise only when:

a. The Institution and the Licensor have accepted a written Order Form incorporating this Agreement.

b. The applicable licence fees have been paid, where payment is required.

c. The Institution has been authorised by the Licensor to access or deploy the Software.

The Order Form shall specify the applicable licensing period, fees, authorised user limits, licensed modules, deployment model and support arrangements.

The Institution's use of the Software shall constitute acceptance of the applicable operational and technical requirements of this Agreement once the licence has been validly executed.

